{"path":"numeric/valarray/exp","title":"std::exp(std::valarray)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>exp<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::valarray)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/exp","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"For each element in va computes e raised to the power equal to the value of the element.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/valarray\">&lt;valarray&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> exp<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>For each element in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">va</span></code> computes <i>e</i> raised to the power equal to the value of the element.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> va\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> value array to apply the operation to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Value array containing <i>e</i> raised by the values in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">va</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unqualified function (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">exp</span></code>) is used to perform the computation. If such function is not available, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/exp\"><span class=\"kw1329\">std::<span class=\"me2\">exp</span></span></a></span></code> is used due to <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a>.\n</p><p>The function can be implemented with the return type different from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>. In this case, the replacement type has the following properties:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> All <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> member functions of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span> are provided.\n</li><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/slice_array\">std::slice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/gslice_array\">std::gslice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/mask_array\">std::mask_array</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/indirect_array\">std::indirect_array</a></span> can be constructed from the replacement type.\n</li><li> For every function taking a <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx11\"><span>except <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/begin2\"><code>begin()</code></a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/end2\"><code>end()</code></a></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></span></span>, identical functions taking the replacement types shall be added;\n</li><li> For every function taking two <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> arguments, identical functions taking every combination of <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> and replacement types shall be added.\n</li><li> The return type does not add more than two levels of template nesting over the most deeply-nested argument type.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nvalarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> exp<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> other <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> va<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> i <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> other<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> exp<span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> other<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// proxy object may be returned</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>This example demonstrates the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler%27s_identity\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">Euler's identity <span class=\"texhtml\">e<span class=\"t-su\">iπ<br></span> = -1</span></a> and the related exponents.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;numbers&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;valarray&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> pi <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/constants\"><span class=\"kw3345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numbers</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">pi</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> v <span class=\"sy1\">=</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, pi <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, pi<span class=\"br0\">}</span>, <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> pi <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> pi<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> v2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/exp\"><span class=\"kw1329\">std::<span class=\"me2\">exp</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/showpos\"><span class=\"kw1787\">std::<span class=\"me2\">showpos</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> n <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> v2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>(+1.000000,+0.000000)\n(+0.000000,+1.000000)\n(-1.000000,+0.000000)\n(-0.000000,-1.000000)\n(+1.000000,-0.000000)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/log\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>log<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\">std::log</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/exp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>exp</span><span>expf</span><span>expl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns <span class=\"texhtml\">e</span> raised to the given power (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small e^x}\">e<sup>x</sup></span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/exp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>exp<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  complex base <i>e</i> exponential <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/valarray","title":"std::valarray"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::exp(std::valarray)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. For each element in va computes e raised to the power equal to the value of the element."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"va"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Value array containing e raised by the values in va."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Unqualified function (exp) is used to perform the computation. If such function is not available, std::exp is used due to argument-dependent lookup."},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Example","note":"This example demonstrates the Euler's identity eiπ = -1 and the related exponents."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"log(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::log to each element of valarray"},{"label":"exp, expf, expl","note":"returns e raised to the given power (ex)"},{"label":"exp(std::complex)","note":"complex base e exponential"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":321,"codeBlockCount":3}
